{"sourceSha256": "27ca8fcbd245f848caa354bd05407aefef9e5968dcb5ed6fb071a70da4c28644", "text": "ra\n@F | | SPEAKING SUB-TEST\n\nROLE PLAYER'S CARD NO. 8 NURSING\n\nSETTING — Hospital ward\n\n|PATIENT You are a 35 year-old patient who had abdominal surgery four days ago for removal of a\nlarge benign tumour. Severe abdominal pain and vomiting over two days prompted you to\nhave tests done as you are usually in good health. You had been suffering intermittent\nabdominal pain for about three months. Your recovery from the operation has been\ncomplicated by a wound infection, Now, you are anwdous that not all of the mass was\nfound and you are worrying that the tumour may have been malignant\n\nAsk the nurse whether it's possible that the turnour was malignant. How could\nshe/ he be certain?\n\nDon't be easily reassured. Express your concern that not all of the tumour mass\nwas removed\n\nAsk how much longer you will need to stay in hospital, Is it possible the tumour\nwill reappear? When can you recommence your cycling routine?\n\n| CANDIDATE'S CARD NURSING\n\nSETTING — Hospital ward\n\n\\NURSE The patient is a 35 year-old who had abdominal surgery four days ago for removal of a\nlarge benign tumour. Now, in the fourth day afler surgery, her/ his recovery has been\ncomplicated by a wound infection, The infection is minor, but the patient appears anmous\n\n|TASK Reassure the patient about the certainty of the diagnostic process for tumours\n\nTry to calm the patient by explaining the infection is not serious, Make some\nsuggestions to make her/ him more comfortable (eq. More pillows, bed\nreadjustment), Check the patient knows how to readjust her/ his bed\n\nAnswer the patient's questions and deal with the patient's anxialy about the\ntumour", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "ra\n@F | | SPEAKING SUB-TEST\n\nROLE PLAYER'S CARD NO. 8 NURSING\n\nSETTING — Hospital ward\n\n|PATIENT You are a 35 year-old patient who had abdominal surgery four days ago for removal of a\nlarge benign tumour. Severe abdominal pain and vomiting over two days prompted you to\nhave tests done as you are usually in good health. You had been suffering intermittent\nabdominal pain for about three months. Your recovery from the operation has been\ncomplicated by a wound infection, Now, you are anwdous that not all of the mass was\nfound and you are worrying that the tumour may have been malignant\n\nAsk the nurse whether it's possible that the turnour was malignant. How could\nshe/ he be certain?\n\nDon't be easily reassured. Express your concern that not all of the tumour mass\nwas removed\n\nAsk how much longer you will need to stay in hospital, Is it possible the tumour\nwill reappear? When can you recommence your cycling routine?\n\n| CANDIDATE'S CARD NURSING\n\nSETTING — Hospital ward\n\n\\NURSE The patient is a 35 year-old who had abdominal surgery four days ago for removal of a\nlarge benign tumour. Now, in the fourth day afler surgery, her/ his recovery has been\ncomplicated by a wound infection, The infection is minor, but the patient appears anmous\n\n|TASK Reassure the patient about the certainty of the diagnostic process for tumours\n\nTry to calm the patient by explaining the infection is not serious, Make some\nsuggestions to make her/ him more comfortable (eq. More pillows, bed\nreadjustment), Check the patient knows how to readjust her/ his bed\n\nAnswer the patient's questions and deal with the patient's anxialy about the\ntumour", "extraction": "ocr", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 1972.0, "height": 2800.0, "blocks": [{"text": "ra\n@F | | SPEAKING SUB-TEST", "lines": [{"text": "ra", "x": 0.16531, "y": 0.06286, "width": 0.00963, "height": 0.00714, "confidence": 0.318, "words": [{"text": "ra", "x": 0.16531, "width": 0.00963, "confidence": 0.318}], "uncertainWords": ["ra"]}, {"text": "@F | | SPEAKING SUB-TEST", "x": 0.16531, "y": 0.0625, "width": 0.73276, "height": 0.03036, "confidence": 0.712, "words": [{"text": "@F", "x": 0.16531, "width": 0.07